ops.details:
Add a new package-private final class ElementQueryHelper in the same Element.java file (below the Element class). Implement static methods that contain the moved logic. The helper should be in package org.jsoup.nodes and reuse existing imports at top of the file. Methods to provide (static):
- Elements select(Element el, String cssQuery) { return Selector.select(cssQuery, el); }
- Elements select(Element el, Evaluator evaluator) { return Selector.select(evaluator, el); }
- Stream<Element> selectStream(Element el, String cssQuery) { return Selector.selectStream(cssQuery, el); }
- Stream<Element> selectStream(Element el, Evaluator eval) { return Selector.selectStream(eval, el); }
- Element selectFirst(Element el, String cssQuery) { return Selector.selectFirst(cssQuery, el); }
- Element selectFirst(Element el, Evaluator evaluator) { return Collector.findFirst(evaluator, el); }
- Elements selectNodes(Element el, String cssQuery) { return selectNodes(el, evaluatorOf(cssQuery), Node.class); }
- <T extends Node> Nodes<T> selectNodes(Element el, Evaluator evaluator, Class<T> type) { Validate.notNull(evaluator); return Collector.collectNodes(evaluator, el, type); }
The helper methods must be package-private (no modifier) or final static, and must not be public. Keep method names as above. Use exactly the classes and methods referenced in the original implementations.
